# UI Architecture

Apply when designing or refactoring UI structure:

## Reuse-First

- Search before creating components, hooks, or CSS classes.
- Extract when the same JSX shell, state/effects, or utility-class chain appears 2+ times.

## Folder Structure

- Feature folders: `common/`, `desktop/`, `mobile/` with a thin root selector.
- Base primitives in `src/components/ui/common/`; section wrappers in section `common/`.
- Hooks in `src/hooks/<responsibility>/`; repeated styles in `src/styles/components/`.

## Viewport Layout (Mandatory)

- Sections are viewport slots only: `height: 100svh; position: relative; overflow: hidden` — no nav-clearing padding.
- Visible content lives in `.section-frame` with `top: var(--section-frame-top, var(--nav-h))`.
- Card height uses `max-height: calc(100svh - var(--nav-h) - var(--section-content-gap))`, not percentages.

Load `.cursor/skills/frontend/ui-architecture/SKILL.md` for the full layout model and extraction rules.
